// If the current SQL prefix is complete, we close the span immediately so the
// final output contains both delimiters. Otherwise we decode constrained SQL:
// when the grammar is narrow we use single-token constrained steps; when it is
// wider we use `ConstrainedSymbol` to emit larger valid SQL units efficiently.
// EOS is always terminal: if a constrained step or symbol hits EOS, we stop
// immediately rather than continuing.
