// parser until completion, and finally deterministically closing the span.
// This directly targets the evaluation requirement that outputs contain << >>,
// while also improving syntax rate because essentially all generation work now
// happens under parser control rather than in unconstrained free text.
// Inside the span, the strategy remains adaptive: at narrow grammar points it
// uses ConstrainedStep plus AppendConstrainedToken for precise token growth,
// and at wider grammar points it uses ConstrainedSymbol to advance multiple
// valid tokens at once. EOS is always terminal, and closing is attempted only
// when parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) is known.
