  //   and currentConstrainedOut becomes [], so generated ends with the empty
  //   constrained suffix immediately. In the constrained-growth branch, we
  //   define stablePrefix by removing the old constrained suffix from generated,
  //   then assign generated := stablePrefix + currentOut and
  //   currentConstrainedOut := currentOut; therefore generated ends with the new
  //   constrained contents by construction. In the manual-close branch we leave
  //   constrained mode, so the implication is vacuous.
  //
  // cost accounting: The manual-open branch appends exactly one token and
  //   increments steps by 1. The constrained-growth branch uses
  //   ConstrainedSymbol, receives stepsUsed, and increments steps by exactly
  //   stepsUsed. The manual-close branch appends exactly one token and
  //   increments steps by 1. Query-only operations such as IsCompletePrefix do
  //   not change steps. We finally assign cost := steps.
  //
  // progress: In the manual-open branch, generated grows by exactly one token
